ially when it was  revealed that there were anti Warren  talking points being used by Bernie  staffers the Bernie campaign said these  were rogue staffers we did not authorize  these talking points that has fallen  apart and  I would be doing something dishonest if  I didn't tell you this the Bernie  Sanders camp has now confirmed that they  were indeed using an anti Warren script  in multiple early states and it's  important because this is different than  the initial story that was told if it is  untrue that Bernie said a woman can't  win it's disgustingly immoral to accuse  him of that but now that Bernie has  admitted that the Sanders campaign did  utilize this anti Warren script and at  least a couple of early voting states  there is something else here that Warren  can rightly be critical of Bernie for  doing but here's the thing if you come  to me and you say David please  adjudicate what's worse is using an anti  Warren script when campaigning worse or  is falsely claiming that Bernie said a  woman can't win worse well if it's a lie  claiming that Bernie said a woman can't  win is worse for sure because the  reality is that the anti Warren script  that Bernie deployed framing Elizabeth  Warren as the candidate for the educated  elites it's not morally wrong to do that  this is politics now the issue is Bernie  and Warren seem to have agreed back in  2018 not to attack each other and by  deploying the anti Warren script Bernie  Sanders broke his agreement with  Elizabeth Warren that's between them  though right that's for them to figure  out this is politics scripts that go  after other candidates during phone  banking and door-knocking  are used all the time the issue for us  to figure out because our priority is  removing Donald Trump is whether any of  this helps us do that when Bernie  Sanders uses a script that attacks  Elizabeth Warren in early States does  that jeopardize the likelihood of  removing Donald Trump if Bernie is not  ultimately the nominee maybe it does  when a story is put out by CNN with or  without confirmation by Elizabeth Warren  we don't know coordination with  Elizabeth Warren rather she confirmed it  but was there coordination there we  don't know if neither burning or warren  are the nominees what does the  this dust-up do for our chance to defeat  Donald Trump that's why I've said from  the beginning I do not want this to get  ugly in a way that helps Donald Trump  it's starting to get ugly in a way that  may help Donald Trump now I'll be honest  I think all of this scandal this week  does nothing to propel Bernie nor  Elizabeth Warren into first place and by  so buying time for Joe Biden to remain  in first place it positions Biden to  start winning primaries which may have  been the goal of all of this thing from  the beginning let me know what you think  I'm on Twitter follow me there and send  me a message letting me know what you  think is the ultimate goal of all of  this and who is the real catalyst for  this is this an establishment plan is  this a war an establishment plan is it a  warren Biden plan is it truly just  innocent stories coming to light  increasingly that's hard to believe let  me know what you think I'm on Twitter at  D Pakman
 

